            {
              "message": "P1 upstream restatement: `domain::DocString`, `domain::TypeEntry`, `domain::TraitEntry`, and `domain::FunctionEntry` docs restate the lint-conformance ADR/spec behavior in prose, including why fields are private, why `docs` becomes `Option<DocString>`, and the constructor/accessor strategy. Per `knowledge/conventions/no-upstream-restatement.md`, these catalogue docs should cite IN-13/IN-14/AC-14..AC-16 rather than restating the upstream contract.",
              "severity": "P1",
              "file": "track/items/catalog-generation-annotation-2026-07-04/domain-types.json",
              "line": 143,
              "category": "upstream_restatement"
            },
            {
              "message": "P1 upstream restatement: multiple usecase entries restate spec behavior instead of only anchoring it. Examples include `usecase::CatalogGateContext` spelling out phase2/merge/commit strictness, `usecase::CatalogCheckVerdict` restating exit semantics, and `usecase::CatalogError` restating per-variant AC/D decision behavior. This duplicates the upstream spec/ADR contract in the type catalogue docs.",
              "severity": "P1",
              "file": "track/items/catalog-generation-annotation-2026-07-04/usecase-types.json",
              "line": 19,
              "category": "upstream_restatement"
            },
            {
              "message": "P1 upstream restatement: infrastructure catalogue docs restate upstream D4/CN-02 behavior. `infrastructure::FsCatalogAdapter`, `infrastructure::CatalogDraftError`, `scan_todo_holes`, and `try_complete` describe schema authority, `$todo` traversal, completion-boundary behavior, and consumer impact in prose instead of leaving those behaviors to the cited anchors.",
              "severity": "P1",
              "file": "track/items/catalog-generation-annotation-2026-07-04/infrastructure-types.json",
              "line": 15,
              "category": "upstream_restatement"
            },
            {
              "message": "P1 upstream restatement: CLI catalogue docs restate command behavior from the spec/ADR, especially the D8/IN-11 track-id guard and read/write resolution rules in `cli::CatalogInitArgs` and `cli::commands::catalog::execute`. These docs should identify the surface and cite IN-11/AC-09 rather than reproducing the fail-closed contract.",
              "severity": "P1",
              "file": "track/items/catalog-generation-annotation-2026-07-04/cli-types.json",
              "line": 84,
              "category": "upstream_restatement"
            },
            {
              "message": "P1 upstream restatement: cli_driver DTO docs restate upstream validation and guard behavior, such as `CatalogInitInput` describing the D8 write guard and `CatalogAddInput`/`CatalogCiteInput` describing downstream validation semantics. The type catalogue should cite the relevant anchors instead of duplicating the behavior contract.",
