        {
          "type": "final",
          "verdict": "findings_remain",
          "findings": [
            {
              "message": "The `docs` fields for domain catalogue entries such as `domain::TodoInstruction`, `domain::DraftHole`, `domain::CatalogImportAction`, `domain::TypeEntry`, `domain::TraitEntry`, and `domain::FunctionEntry` restate upstream ADR/spec behavior in prose instead of only citing the upstream anchors. For example, `TodoInstruction` re-describes how `$todo` nodes are generated and consumed. `knowledge/conventions/no-upstream-restatement.md` applies to `<layer>-types.json` docs, so these downstream restatements should be replaced with concise entry identification plus anchor cites.",
              "severity": "P1",
              "file": "track/items/catalog-generation-annotation-2026-07-04/domain-types.json",
              "line": 21,
              "category": "SoT integrity / upstream restatement"
            },
            {
              "message": "The usecase catalogue has the same upstream-restatement problem across keys including `usecase::CatalogGateContext`, `usecase::CatalogAddCommand`, `usecase::CatalogError`, `usecase::CatalogInteractor`, `usecase::CatalogService`, and `usecase::CatalogPort`. These docs repeat gate semantics, validation ownership, error semantics, track guard behavior, and port wiring rationale that already live in ADR/spec anchors. Per `knowledge/conventions/no-upstream-restatement.md`, the docs must cite anchors rather than re-explain the behavioral contract.",
              "severity": "P1",
              "file": "track/items/catalog-generation-annotation-2026-07-04/usecase-types.json",
              "line": 19,
              "category": "SoT integrity / upstream restatement"
            },
            {
              "message": "CLI catalogue docs for keys such as `cli::CatalogKindArg`, `cli::CatalogAddArgs`, `cli::CatalogCheckArgs`, `cli::CatalogCommand`, and `cli::commands::catalog::execute` restate clap spelling, argument mapping, track-id guard behavior, dispatch, and exit-code behavior in prose. Those are upstream behavior contracts already covered by spec refs; keeping the narrative here violates `knowledge/conventions/no-upstream-restatement.md` and creates another drift source.",
              "severity": "P1",
              "file": "track/items/catalog-generation-annotation-2026-07-04/cli-types.json",
              "line": 21,
              "category": "SoT integrity / upstream restatement"
            },
            {
              "message": "The cli_driver catalogue docs for `cli_driver::CatalogKindSelect`, `cli_driver::CatalogAddInput`, `cli_driver::CatalogCheckInput`, `cli_driver::CatalogInput`, and `cli_driver::CatalogDriver` restate boundary conversion, dynamic layer handling, trusted track-id handling, and dispatch behavior. These should be anchor-backed type declarations, not prose copies of the upstream contract, under `knowledge/conventions/no-upstream-restatement.md`.",
              "severity": "P1",
              "file": "track/items/catalog-generation-annotation-2026-07-04/cli_driver-types.json",
              "line": 21,
              "category": "SoT integrity / upstream restatement"
