    "adr": {
      "rounds": [
        {
          "type": "fast",
          "verdict": "findings_remain",
          "findings": [
            {
              "message": "`knowledge/adr/2026-07-02-1345-catalogue-generation-annotation.md` lets `sotp catalog` auto-resolve the current track *and* accept `--track-id` as an override for `add/import/cite`. Those commands write under `track/items/<id>/`, so that wording conflicts with the established write-safety rule in [track-id default ADR](/home/flip451/individual/t-rust/templates/SoTOHE-core/knowledge/adr/2026-05-26-1813-track-id-default-active-track.md#L149-L157), which requires write operations to fail closed on a branch/id mismatch rather than allow cross-track overrides.",
              "severity": "P1",
              "file": "/home/flip451/individual/t-rust/templates/SoTOHE-core/knowledge/adr/2026-07-02-1345-catalogue-generation-annotation.md",
              "line": 125,
              "category": "inconsistent decision"
            },
            {
              "message": "The phase-2 command surface is still missing an explicit way to supply a new type's own `generics` / `where` bounds. D1 says the catalog must preserve that information, but D6/D8 only expose member-level Rust signatures plus rustdoc import. As written, downstream tooling cannot unambiguously author or validate generic-bearing structs, traits, or impl blocks unless that encoding is stated somewhere explicit.",
              "severity": "P1",
              "file": "/home/flip451/individual/t-rust/templates/SoTOHE-core/knowledge/adr/2026-07-02-1345-catalogue-generation-annotation.md",
              "line": 102,
              "category": "decision underspecified for downstream consumption"
            }
          ],
          "hash": "rvw1:sha256:f1b3a8acf5cdabbe3899f7ed923fa8988ccc28c9bbe4532a5a92165a5699bb13",
          "at": "2026-07-04T01:38:00Z"
        },
        {
          "type": "fast",
          "verdict": "findings_remain",
          "findings": [
            {
              "message": "`D7` wires `sotp catalog check` into both the Phase 2 gate and the commit gate, but it never says whether that check is skipped or downgraded when a catalog file is still absent or only partially filled. As written, that reintroduces the Phase 0/1 commit-blocking behavior that `knowledge/adr/2026-06-01-0406-review-gate-tolerate-missing-catalogue.md` explicitly removed, and it also conflicts with `knowledge/adr/2026-06-16-1030-signal-gate-strictness-config.md`, which keeps TDDD catalogue-impl checks `interim` at commit time. The commit-gate semantics here are therefore inconsistent and underspecified.",
              "severity": "P1",
              "file": "/home/flip451/individual/t-rust/templates/SoTOHE-core/knowledge/adr/2026-07-02-1345-catalogue-generation-annotation.md",
              "line": 110,
              "category": "consistency"
            }
          ],
          "hash": "rvw1:sha256:a7f734059dc8bcceb5d7baeac55f36522a204d62a6c3a43e6160c444741cdf7a",
          "at": "2026-07-04T01:45:50Z"
        },
        {
          "type": "fast",
          "verdict": "findings_remain",
          "findings": [
            {
              "message": "`catalog check` is coupled to a mandatory `.harness/config/signal-gates.json` and treats missing/malformed gate config as a hard failure. That turns a user-owned signal-gate setting into a framework-enforced prerequisite, which conflicts with `knowledge/conventions/responsibility-boundary.md`'s rule that signal-gate settings are provide+docs only, not CI-enforced. Downstream forks that intentionally omit the file will now be blocked before any catalogue work can run.",
              "severity": "P1",
              "file": "/home/flip451/individual/t-rust/templates/SoTOHE-core/knowledge/adr/2026-07-02-1345-catalogue-generation-annotation.md",
              "line": 116,
              "category": "scope_leakage"
            }
          ],
          "hash": "rvw1:sha256:ddc0e82f9f351b7cb33b5b2746a708e42c4accc2cf9722956288ab52089be2a8",
          "at": "2026-07-04T01:51:03Z"
