              "line": 17,
              "category": "task description non-executable"
            },
            {
              "message": "`T005`/`T006`/`T007` mix the implementation target with upstream behavior and rationale prose (`single place a draft crosses`, `schema authority`, `strict block`). That is the kind of restatement `knowledge/conventions/no-upstream-restatement.md` forbids.",
              "severity": "P1",
              "file": "/home/flip451/individual/t-rust/templates/SoTOHE-core/track/items/catalog-generation-annotation-2026-07-04/impl-plan.json",
              "line": 29,
              "category": "upstream restatement"
            },
            {
              "message": "`T008` and `T009` omit an anchor cite, so the executable boundary is left implicit and the implementer has to infer the split from prose. That is non-executable under the scope policy.",
              "severity": "P1",
              "file": "/home/flip451/individual/t-rust/templates/SoTOHE-core/track/items/catalog-generation-annotation-2026-07-04/impl-plan.json",
              "line": 47,
              "category": "task description non-executable"
            },
            {
