        {
          "type": "fast",
          "verdict": "findings_remain",
          "findings": [
            {
              "message": "Joining raw `track_id` here lets `../` or absolute inputs escape `items_dir`, and every verb reuses this helper before any root check. That creates a workspace traversal boundary break; validate `track_id` as a `TrackId` and verify the resolved directory stays under the trusted root.",
              "severity": "P0",
              "file": "/home/flip451/individual/t-rust/templates/SoTOHE-core/libs/infrastructure/src/tddd/catalog_gen/fs_access.rs",
              "line": 40,
              "category": "trusted-root violation"
            },
            {
              "message": "Catalogue I/O follows whatever path this helper returns with `read_to_string`/`write`, but it never rejects symlinked leaves or ancestors. A symlinked `*-types.json` can redirect reads and writes outside the workspace; reject symlinks at the boundary like the other infra loaders do.",
              "severity": "P0",
              "file": "/home/flip451/individual/t-rust/templates/SoTOHE-core/libs/infrastructure/src/tddd/catalog_gen/fs_access.rs",
              "line": 81,
              "category": "symlink not rejected at boundary"
            },
            {
              "message": "`unwrap_or_default()` masks all `load_spec_anchors` failures, not just a missing Phase-0 spec. A malformed or unreadable `spec.json` is treated as an empty anchor set, so `check` can proceed instead of failing closed.",
              "severity": "P1",
              "file": "/home/flip451/individual/t-rust/templates/SoTOHE-core/libs/infrastructure/src/tddd/catalog_gen/verb_check.rs",
              "line": 39,
              "category": "non-fail-closed config"
            }
          ],
          "hash": "rvw1:sha256:83b114c3f7e84a5664d7d9e7a458429627f901193fef3474a6c813ba51bf61a8",
          "at": "2026-07-04T13:46:20Z"
        },
        {
          "type": "fast",
          "verdict": "findings_remain",
          "findings": [
            {
              "message": "The add/import/cite path reads catalogue files as raw `serde_json::Value` and rewrites them without any `schema_version` probe. That means a v4 or future catalogue is silently mutated instead of being rejected fail-closed, which is the same versioning footgun the strict DTO codecs are meant to prevent.",
              "severity": "P1",
              "file": "/home/flip451/individual/t-rust/templates/SoTOHE-core/libs/infrastructure/src/tddd/catalog_gen/fs_access.rs",
              "line": 115,
              "category": "serde codec break"
            },
            {
              "message": "`check_layer` validates schema only after the `$todo` scan. If a catalogue is on an unsupported schema version but still contains holes, the function returns the hole verdict and never reaches `try_complete`, so the version error is not fail-closed. Commit-mode checks can therefore downgrade a schema break to an interim warning.",
              "severity": "P1",
              "file": "/home/flip451/individual/t-rust/templates/SoTOHE-core/libs/infrastructure/src/tddd/catalog_gen/verb_check.rs",
              "line": 77,
              "category": "serde codec break"
            }
          ],
          "hash": "rvw1:sha256:5fc7ad9903529f2278e5b5af04177aa9717e6329c21b0e01472676f54859b0c2",
          "at": "2026-07-04T14:07:27Z"
